Reason: a view that draws into its own surface (AM2R 1.5.5 widescreen) was cleared only when the room draws its
background colour, while the screen is always cleared. Where a room leaves pixels undrawn (the filler gap left of
rm_a1h03 in 16:9), old frames smeared as the camera moved and shots left trails.
Upstream: Engine bug on every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

diff --git a/src/runner.c b/src/runner.c
--- a/src/runner.c
+++ b/src/runner.c
@@ -1309,8 +1309,8 @@
 
                 Runner_surfaceSetTarget(runner, view->surfaceId);
 
-                if (runner->drawBackgroundColor)
-                    renderer->vtable->clearScreen(renderer, runner->currentRoom->backgroundColor, 1.0f);
+                // Cleared like the screen above: whatever the room leaves undrawn would otherwise smear the last frames.
+                renderer->vtable->clearScreen(renderer, runner->drawBackgroundColor ? runner->currentRoom->backgroundColor : 0, 1.0f);
 
                 runner->viewCurrent = (int32_t) vi;
                 runner->renderer->cameraCurrent = runner->views[runner->viewCurrent].cameraId;
